      "message": "nit: we can just return here?\n\nActually it could be simplified to the following then?\n\n```\n\thash_for_each_possible(iommu_domain_hasht, domain, hnode, pgd)\n\t\tif (domain-\u003epgd \u003d\u003d pgd \u0026\u0026 atomic_inc_not_zero(\u0026domain-\u003erefcount))\n\t\t\treturn domain;\n\n\treturn NULL;\n```\n\n...Hmm, actually atomic_inc_not_zero() shouldn\u0027t return true here unless we have a bug? So maybe something like this?\n\n```\n\thash_for_each_possible(iommu_domain_hasht, domain, hnode, pgd) {\n\t\tif (domain-\u003epgd !\u003d pgd)\n\t\t\tcontinue;\n\n\t\tif (WARN_ON_ONCE(!atomic_inc_not_zero(\u0026domain-\u003erefcount))\n\t\t\treturn NULL;\n\n\t\treturn domain;\n\t}\n\n\treturn NULL;\n```",
